{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["And it produced blossoms, and it budded a flower, and it ripened almonds — it appears by the plain sense: when Moshe took it out, he found that it had blossomed and nothing more, as it is written: והנה פרח מטה אהרן, but afterwards:" "And it budded a flower — before the eyes of all Israel. And afterwards: and it ripened almonds. For had the matter been so from the start, then neither the blossoming nor the budding would have been visible, and also it would not have been necessary to write והנה פרח, but rather והנה גמל שקדים מטה אהרן לבית לוי."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:27.343325001Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}